 
Working Principle - 
A piezoelectric actuator plays a crucial role in dynamically adjusting the shape of the membrane, which serves as the foundation for the attached mirror. This adjustment 
is achieved by applying a controlled voltage input, which induces a mechanical deformation in the actuator due to the piezoelectric effect. As the voltage varies, 
the actuator expands or contracts, causing precise modifications in the membrane’s surface profile. These adjustments enable real-time control over the mirror’s curvature 
and alignment, making the system highly responsive to operational requirements. Such fine-tuned control is particularly essential in applications requiring high-precision 
laser machining, ensuring optimal performance and minimizing optical distortions.






